 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Underlying currency exposure limit
+
+If you trade multiple pairs that are priced against, or settled in, the same underlying currency - for example several `BTC`-margined futures, or several pairs quoted in the same stablecoin - a large adverse move in that one underlying currency can hit several of your open trades at once.
+
+`max_underlying_currency_exposure` limits this concentration risk by capping the combined stake committed to all *simultaneously open* trades that share a pair's quote/settlement currency, as a ratio of the [tradable capital](#tradable-balance).
+
+For example, with a tradable balance of 1000 USDT and `max_underlying_currency_exposure=0.5`, the bot will allow at most 500 USDT to be committed at once across all open trades quoted in USDT (e.g. `BTC/USDT`, `ETH/USDT`, ...) - regardless of how many free trade slots or how much stake_amount would otherwise be used. A pair quoted in a different currency (e.g. `ETH/BTC`) is tracked against its own, independent limit.
+
+When opening a new trade would exceed the limit, the bot will reduce the stake amount to whatever headroom remains for that underlying currency, or skip the trade entirely if no headroom remains. This is evaluated identically for live/dry-run and backtesting, since both go through the same sizing logic.
+
+This is a [Strategy Override](#parameters-in-the-strategy) value - it can be set in the configuration or as a strategy attribute. It is disabled (no limit) by default.
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
